    "description": "All aspects of software development/sustainment activities including requirements definition, system/subsystem design, code writing, code testing (unit test), subsystem test, documentation (system specifications/subsystem specifications, as-built design documents, software description documents, interface control documents, test procedures, test reports, acceptance test packages and procedures, functional configuration audits, physical configuration audits), selloff, etc. Technical program management including Earned Value management technical program measures. Worked in a CMM/CMMI Level 5 organization  for two decades while with the 309th Software Maintenance Group at Hill Air Force Base.  Prepared and presented program management review presentations.\nAlso served as a representative to the extended software engineering process group which controlled organizational process development, implementation and performance tracking.\nActed as the \"New Worklaod Development\" point of contact for the software group, interfacing with multiple current, future and potential customers to identify thier requirments, our capabilities, and the common areas in which we could work together.",
